  "candidate_definition": "33 domain-specific supervised rating/recommendation datasets, one raw review JSONL.gz artifact per category.",
  "task_and_architecture": "Ratings (1-5), user IDs, parent item IDs and timestamps form a direct supervised rating-regression/classification task after text/images are excluded. A plain dense MLP can represent user/item categories via one-hot features, but dense user/item input width ranges from thousands to tens of millions, which makes the registered `[512]*5` full-batch profile infeasible for most categories. For the smallest categories it may fit activation-only estimates; however rights fail before an empirical difficulty pilot.",
  "splits": "Official 2023 benchmark scripts advertise 0-core and 5-core processed datasets, per-user leave-last-out train/validation/test splits, and timestamp-based 8:1:1 train/validation/test at fixed global cut points. Exact category splits were not downloaded/parsed in this audit.",
  "rights": "No dataset license is stated on the official card/page; it identifies itself as research-collected and carries McAuley Lab copyright. The linked MIT license applies to benchmark-processing code, not the review data. Permissive data reuse therefore remains unverified; all categories are crossed out under the strict open-license criterion.",
  "probe_method": "Unauthenticated HTTP GET with Range bytes=0-0 against every official category review artifact; stream closed without retaining payload.",
